            <ArticleTitle>[Occupational asthma].</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>1972-1975</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Occupational asthma is the most common occupational respiratory disease. It mainly affects young workers with significant socio-economic consequences. Early recognition improves its prognosis. A rigorous investigative approach while the worker is still exposed at work and appropriate medical care require a multi-disciplinary collaboration. Prevention is the key element in the management of professional asthma.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
